======== ROUND 1
['# Task\nYou are given a review of a scientific paper. Your task is to classify whether the review recommends accepting the paper ("Yes") or rejecting it ("No"). To do this, consider the overall sentiment of the review, including whether the reviewer finds the work technically sound, valuable, and well-presented, or if they highlight significant weaknesses, limitations, or concerns that would justify rejection.\n\nFocus on the general tone and conclusion of the review:\n- If the review is predominantly positive and suggests the paper is good or excellent, choose "Yes".\n- If the review is predominantly negative, criticizes the work, or indicates the paper is not suitable for acceptance, choose "No".\n\nRespond with: "Yes" or "No". \n\n# Output format\nAnswer Yes or No as labels\n\n# Prediction\nText: {{ text }}\nLabel:', '# Task\nGiven the review text, determine whether the paper should be accepted (Yes) or rejected (No). Focus on the overall quality, novelty, evaluation rigor, and clarity of the work, considering the detailed content, strengths, weaknesses, and limitations described in the review. Do not solely rely on superficial cues; assess the technical soundness and the thoroughness of the evaluation as presented. \n\n# Output format\nAnswer Yes or No as labels\n\n# Prediction\nText: {{ text }}\nLabel:', '# Task\nGiven the review text, determine whether the overall assessment warrants acceptance (Yes) or rejection (No). Focus on the review\'s evaluation of the paper\'s novelty, technical rigor, experimental validation, and clarity. Consider whether the review provides sufficient evidence to support a positive or negative judgment. Your answer should be "Yes" if the review indicates the paper should be accepted, or "No" if it suggests rejection. \n\n# Output format\nAnswer Yes or No as labels\n\n# Prediction\nText: {{ text }}\nLabel:', '# Task\nRead the following review carefully. Based on its content, decide whether the reviewer recommends acceptance ("Yes") or rejection ("No") of the paper. Focus on the reviewer\'s overall assessment, comments on strengths and weaknesses, and the final rating to inform your decision.\n\nReview Text:\n[Insert review here]\n\nRespond with:\n- "Yes" if the review favors acceptance.\n- "No" if it favors rejection.\nAvoid additional explanations or comments. \n\n# Output format\nAnswer Yes or No as labels\n\n# Prediction\nText: {{ text }}\nLabel:']
